<title>FRANCE: Paris Airports import traffic down 0.2pct Jan-Aug.</title>
<headline>Paris Airports import traffic down 0.2pct Jan-Aug.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-August 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 338,240 tonnes, a decrease of 0.2 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>January-August 1996 traffic from North America, the principal region of origin for ADP imports, rose by 3.2 percent on 1995 levels to 120,083 tonnes in contrast to Far East-originating cargo which fell two percent to 72,467 tonnes.</p>
<p>ADP import traffic from sub-Saharan Africa rose by 7.7 percent on the first eight months of 1995 to 35,394 tonnes.</p>
<p>Global January-August 1996 ADP import traffic, by region, with percentage change on January-August 1995, was as follows:  Domestic		  19,846 tonnes    down 13.2pct</p>
<p> European Union	  39,440 tonnes    up    2.9</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	    7,306 tonnes    up    5.9</p>
<p> North Africa	     7,139 tonnes    down 11.9</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa    35,394 tonnes    up    7.7</p>
<p> North America	  120,083 tonnes    up    3.2</p>
<p> French territories     8,457 tonnes    down  4.4</p>
<p> Latin America	   12,024 tonnes    down  5.2</p>
<p> Middle East	     16,084 tonnes    down  2.7</p>
<p> Far East		  72,467 tonnes    down  2.0</p>
<p> Total		    338,240 tonnes    down  0.2</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
